#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:116
msgid "Pre-processing"
msgstr "Prétraitement"

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:118
msgid ""
"The :guilabel:`PRC` tab defines how the images are corrected and masked "
"before they are added to the time series. Its content depends on the "
"**Type** selected in the :guilabel:`SRC` tab."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:122
msgid "This step is optional; default values are set for every type of data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:125
msgid "Optical"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:127
msgid ""
"For optical data, the panel is a simplified version of the `Composite "
"<optical_mosaic.html#composite>`__ panel of the **Optical mosaic** "
"recipe: as every acquisition is kept, there is no composing method, no "
"pixel filters and no cloud buffering. The panel opens in a **simple** "
"view; select :guilabel:`More` to reveal the **advanced** options (and "
":guilabel:`Less` to hide them again)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:131
msgid "By default, SEPAL applies:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:133
msgid "Corrections: **None** (top-of-atmosphere reflectance is used)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:134
#, fuzzy
msgid "Cloud masking: **Moderate**"
msgstr "Masquage de nuage: :guilabel:`modéré`"

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:135
#, fuzzy
msgid "Snow/ice masking: **On**"
msgstr "Masquage des neiges: :guilabel:`activé`"

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:141
#, fuzzy
msgid "**Corrections**"
msgstr "**Correction**"

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:143
msgid ""
":guilabel:`SR`: Uses the atmospherically corrected surface reflectance of"
" the scenes instead of the top-of-atmosphere (TOA) reflectance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:144
msgid ""
":guilabel:`BRDF`: Corrects for bidirectional reflectance distribution "
"function (BRDF) effects. In the advanced view, the **BRDF Multiplier** "
"field controls how much correction is applied: the higher the value, the "
"stronger the correction (default **4**)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:145
msgid ""
":guilabel:`Calibrate`: Calibrates the bands to improve the consistency "
"between sensors. In a time series, calibration is always applied when "
"**SR** is not selected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:147
msgid "**Cloud masking**"
msgstr "**Masquage des nuages**"

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:149
msgid "In the simple view, choose a preset:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:151
#, fuzzy
msgid ":guilabel:`Moderate`: Standard cloud masking."
msgstr ""
":guilabel:`Modéré`: Ne comptez que sur les bandes QA des images sources "
"pour le masquage des nuages."

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:152
msgid ""
":guilabel:`Aggressive`: Uses the same algorithms with stricter "
"thresholds. It masks more clouds, but may also mask built-up areas and "
"other bright features."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:153
msgid ""
":guilabel:`Custom`: Automatically selected when you fine-tune the "
"individual cloud-masking algorithms in the advanced view."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:155
msgid ""
"In the advanced view, you can add and configure the individual cloud-"
"masking algorithms (**SEPAL Cloud Score**, **S2 Cloud Score+**, **S2 "
"Cloud Probability**, **Landsat CFMask** and **Pino 26**). The available "
"algorithms depend on the selected datasets: the S2 algorithms require "
"Sentinel-2, **Landsat CFMask** requires Landsat, and **Pino 26** requires"
" Sentinel-2 only, without **SR**. They are described in the `Cloud "
"masking <optical_mosaic.html#cloud-masking>`__ section of the **Optical "
"mosaic** recipe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:157
msgid "**Sentinel-2 overlap (advanced view)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:159
msgid ""
"Shown only when Sentinel-2 is selected. Sentinel-2 acquisitions overlap "
"both between orbits and between neighbouring tiles, which can result in "
"duplicated observations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:161
msgid ""
"**Orbit overlap**: :guilabel:`Keep` the overlap between Sentinel-2 orbits"
" or :guilabel:`Remove` it. Defaults to **Keep**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:162
msgid ""
"**Tile overlap**: :guilabel:`Keep` the overlap between Sentinel-2 tiles, "
":guilabel:`Quick remove` most of it, or :guilabel:`Remove` all of it. "
"Defaults to **Quick remove**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:164
msgid "**Snow/ice masking (advanced view)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:166
msgid ""
":guilabel:`On`: Masks snow. This tends to leave some pixels with shadowy "
"snow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:167
msgid ""
":guilabel:`Off`: Doesn't mask snow. Note that some clouds might get "
"misclassified as snow; therefore, disabling snow masking might lead to "
"cloud artifacts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:170
msgid "Radar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:172
msgid ""
"For radar data, the panel contains the same options as the `Options "
"<radar_mosaic.html#options>`__ panel of the **Radar mosaic** recipe "
"(orbits, geometric correction, speckle filters, outlier removal, orbit "
"overlap, border noise correction and minimum observations). Refer to that"
" article for a description of each option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:176
msgid ""
"The defaults differ from the radar mosaic recipe, to keep each "
"acquisition close to the original data:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:178
msgid "Orbits: **Ascending** and **Descending**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:179
msgid "Geometric correction: **Ellipsoid**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:180
msgid "Spatial speckle filter: **None**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:181
msgid "Multitemporal speckle filter: **None**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:182
msgid "Outlier removal: **None**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:185
msgid "Planet"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:187
msgid "For Planet data, the panel contains the following options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:189
msgid ""
"**Cloud masking**: Planet composites already remove clouds. Use this "
"slider to remove additional clouds: the higher the value, the more pixels"
" are masked as clouds. At **0%**, no additional clouds are removed. "
"Defaults to **85%**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:190
msgid ""
"**Cloud buffering**: :guilabel:`None`, :guilabel:`Moderate` (an "
"additional **120 m** around each larger cloud) or :guilabel:`Aggressive` "
"(an additional **600 m**). Defaults to **None**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:191
msgid ""
"**Histogram matching** (only shown for **Daily imagery**): "
":guilabel:`Enabled` normalizes the images using histogram matching. This "
"slows down processing significantly and can cause some details to be "
"lost, but can significantly improve the overall consistency and noise "
"level. Defaults to **Disabled**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:194
msgid "Analysis"
msgstr "Analyse"

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:196
msgid ""
"Once all the parameters are set, you can plot the time series of a pixel "
"using the :btn:`<fa-solid fa-chart-area>` button in the upper-right "
"corner of the map."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:200
msgid ""
"The button is only enabled when the parameters are complete. If it is "
"disabled, check your parameters, as some might be missing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:203
msgid "Plot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:205
msgid ""
"Select :btn:`<fa-solid fa-chart-area>` to start the plotting tool. Move "
"the pointer to the main map; the pointer will be transformed into a :icon"
":`fa-solid fa-plus`. Click anywhere in the AOI to plot the observations "
"of this specific location in a pop-up window."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:207
msgid ""
"The coordinates of the selected point are displayed in the header of the "
"window. Select :btn:`<fa-solid fa-copy>` next to them to copy them to the"
" clipboard."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:208
msgid ""
"Select the band or index to display in the dropdown list in the upper-"
"left corner. The available bands are the same as in the **Retrieve** "
"panel (see `Bands to retrieve`_)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:209
msgid ""
"On the chart, each dot represents one valid observation (i.e. one that "
"was not masked by the pre-processing). Hover over a dot to display its "
"**Date** and **Observation** value. Values are scaled: optical values by "
"10,000 (e.g. an NDVI of 0.6 is displayed as 6000), radar **VV** and "
"**VH** by 100, and **ratio_VV_VH** by 1,000."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:210
msgid ""
"Drag the handles of the range selector below the chart to zoom in on a "
"period."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:211
msgid ""
"Select :btn:`<fa-solid fa-download> Export CSV` in the lower-left corner "
"to download the observations of the selected band as a :code:`.csv` file,"
" named :code:`<recipe name>_<band>_<latitude>_<longitude>.csv`. The file "
"covers the whole period, even if you zoomed in on the chart, and contains"
" the values as displayed on the chart."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:213
msgid "Select :guilabel:`Close` (or press :kbd:`Esc`) to close the window."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:221
msgid ""
"The plot retrieves the information from GEE on the fly. Depending on the "
"number of observations and the selected pre-processing parameters, this "
"can take some time; a spinner is displayed while the data are loading. If"
" the pixel has no valid observation, the message **Pixel has no "
"observations** is displayed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:224
msgid "Retrieve"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:228
msgid ""
"You cannot retrieve a time series to your SEPAL workspace without a small"
" computation quota. If you are a new user, see :doc:`../setup/resource`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:230
msgid ""
"In the upper-right corner, select the :btn:`<fa-solid fa-cloud-arrow-"
"down>` button to open the **Retrieve** panel, where you can select the "
"exportation parameters. A time series is always retrieved to your **SEPAL"
" workspace**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:237
msgid "Bands to retrieve"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:239
msgid ""
"Select one or more bands or indexes to export in **Bands to retrieve**. "
"Each band is exported to its own folder (see `Access`_). The available "
"bands depend on the **Type** selected in the :guilabel:`SRC` tab:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:241
msgid ""
"**Optical**: the spectral bands of the selected datasets (e.g. **blue**, "
"**green**, **red**, **nir**, **swir1**, **swir2**) and the spectral "
"indexes computed from them (e.g. **ndvi**, **ndmi**, **ndfi**). For the "
"full list, see :doc:`../feature/optical_bands`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:242
msgid ""
"**Radar**: **VV**, **VH**, **ratio_VV_VH** and **orbit**. For more "
"information, see :doc:`../feature/radar_bands`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:243
msgid ""
"**Planet**: **blue**, **green**, **red** and **nir**, and the indexes "
"**ndvi**, **ndwi**, **evi**, **evi2** and **savi**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:245
msgid ""
"If a **Classification** recipe is selected in the :guilabel:`SRC` tab, "
"the class probability bands (or the regression band) are also available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:249
msgid ""
"There is no fixed rule to the band selection. Each index is more adapted "
"to a set of analyses in a defined biome. The knowledge of the study area,"
" the evolution expected and the careful selection of an adapted measure "
"will improve the quality of downstream analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:252
msgid "Scale"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:254
msgid ""
"You can set a custom scale for exportation by selecting a value in metres"
" (m). The default is **30 m**. Note that requesting a smaller resolution "
"than the native resolution of the data (e.g. 30 m for Landsat, 10 m for "
"Sentinel-2 and Sentinel-1) will not improve the quality of the output, "
"just its size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:257
msgid "Additional outputs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:259
msgid ""
"Select :guilabel:`SITS files` to also create, for every acquisition date,"
" a :code:`.vrt` file that can be read as a data cube by the `sits R "
"package <https://e-sensing.github.io/sitsbook/>`__. This option is off by"
" default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:262
msgid "Destination"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:264
msgid ""
"**Workspace path**: the destination folder in your SEPAL workspace. By "
"default, :code:`downloads/<recipe name>`, or :code:`downloads/<project "
"name>/<recipe name>` if the recipe belongs to a project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:265
msgid ""
"**Filename prefix**: added to the name of every exported file. By "
"default, the recipe name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:267
msgid "Select :guilabel:`More` to show additional export settings:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:269
msgid ""
"**Tile size**: the AOI is split into tiles of this size, in degrees "
"(default **2**). Each tile is exported in its own folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:270
msgid ""
"**Shard size**: the size, in pixels, of the pieces GEE breaks the image "
"into for processing (default **256**)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:271
msgid ""
"**File dimensions multiple**: the maximum size of each exported file, as "
"a multiple of the shard size (default **2**, i.e. files of up to 512 x "
"512 pixels)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:272
msgid ""
"**CRS** and **CRS transform**: the coordinate reference system and, "
"optionally, the affine transform of the exported images."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:274
msgid ""
"The default values are suitable in most cases; reduce the tile or shard "
"size if the export runs out of memory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:276
msgid "Select :guilabel:`Retrieve` to start the export process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:279
msgid "Exportation status"
msgstr "État d'exportation"

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:281
msgid ""
"Follow the export in the **Tasks** tab (lower-left corner). For more "
"information, see :doc:`../feature/tasks`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:283
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The progress of a time series is reported tile by tile (e.g. "
":code:`Exported 40% of tile 1 out of 3.`), followed by :code:`Assembling "
"tile 1 out of 3...` when the files of a tile are being stacked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:286
msgid "Access"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:288
msgid ""
"Once the export is complete, you can access the data in your SEPAL "
"folders. By default, the data are stored in the :code:`downloads` folder "
"using the following format:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:323
msgid ""
"Understanding how images are stored in a time series is only required if "
"you want to manually use them. The SEPAL applications are bound to this "
"tiling system and can digest the information for you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:325
msgid ""
"The data are stored in a folder named after the recipe, with one sub-"
"folder per retrieved band (e.g. :code:`ndvi`). As GEE cannot export an "
"image collection, and as the data are usually too big to be exported at "
"once, SEPAL divides them into smaller pieces and reassembles them in "
":code:`stack.vrt` files:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:327
msgid ""
"**Tiles**: the AOI is divided into tiles of the selected **Tile size** (2"
" degrees by default). Each tile is stored in a folder named with its "
"number, starting at :code:`0`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:328
msgid ""
"**Chunks**: in each tile, the time period is divided into chunks of 3 "
"months, stored in :code:`chunk-<start date>_<end date>` folders. Periods "
"without any imagery are skipped. Each chunk contains one or more "
":code:`.tif` files, as GEE splits large images into pieces identified by "
"a GEE tile ID (e.g. :code:`0000000000-0000000000`). Each file has one "
"band per acquisition date, named with the date (:code:`YYYY-MM-DD`); "
"acquisitions from the same day are merged using their median."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:329
msgid ""
"**Stacks**: in each tile, one :code:`tile-<gee tile id>/stack.vrt` file "
"gathers the files of all chunks for one GEE tile, covering the full time "
"period. The main :code:`stack.vrt` file of the tile then combines all of "
"them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:330
msgid ""
"**Dates**: the :code:`dates.csv` file lists all the observation dates of "
"the tile in chronological order, matching the bands of :code:`stack.vrt`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:331
msgid ""
"**SITS files** (only if selected in `Additional outputs`_): the "
":code:`sits` folder contains, for each tile, one :code:`.vrt` file per "
"GEE tile, band and acquisition date. The band name is written in upper "
"case, with hyphens instead of underscores (e.g. :code:`NDVI`, :code"
":`RATIO-VV-VH`). The files of all bands are stored in the same folder, so"
" they can be loaded as one multi-band cube."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:335
msgid ""
"The dates contained in :code:`dates.csv` can differ from one tile to "
"another, due to data availability and pre-processing filters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:339
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The full folder, with all its files, is required to read the :code:`.vrt`"
" files."
msgstr ""
"Le dossier complet avec une arborescence cohérente est nécessaire pour "
"lire le fichier `.vrt`"

#: ../../source/cookbook/time_series.rst:343
msgid ""
"Now that you have exported the time series to your SEPAL workspace, it "
"can be downloaded to your computer using `file exchange options "
"<../setup/filezilla.html>`__ or used in one of our `Time-series analysis "
"modules <../modules/time-series.html>`__."
